# .NET
# Anchored to the SDK tree rather than a bare `bin/`, which is recursive: it also
# swallowed `infra/bin/infra.ts`, the CDK app entry point that `infra/cdk.json` names.
# The published repo therefore shipped five stack classes with nothing to instantiate
# them -- `cdk synth` failed with "Cannot find module bin/infra.ts" on a clean clone.
sdk/dotnet/**/bin/
sdk/dotnet/**/obj/
examples/dotnet/**/bin/
examples/dotnet/**/obj/
tools/**/bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
*.nupkg

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg

# TypeScript
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test output
coverage/
TestResults/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
# Coverage reports staged for the purpose-binding gate. `coverage/` above already
# catches the per-package directories; this is the aggregate one that CI collects
# cross-language reports into, and it is a directory name generic enough that
# leaving it untracked-but-unignored invites someone to commit a cobertura dump.
artifacts/
